#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Builds the research-style technical report (report.md) from the package's result files, so every
number in the text is traceable to a script output.  Re-run after any change in 02-18.
"""
import os, sys, json, math, csv, time
HERE = os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)); DAB = os.path.dirname(HERE); REPO = os.path.dirname(DAB)
def J(*p):
    f = os.path.join(DAB, *p)
    return json.load(open(f)) if os.path.exists(f) else None
V = J("04_Design_Calculations", "design_values.json"); T = J("02_Topology_Comparison", "topology_comparison.json")
C = J("11_Control_Algorithms", "control_params.json"); SW = J("05_Simulation", "switched_results.json"); SP = J("05_Simulation", "spice", "spice_results.json")
OPT = J("12_Optimization", "optimization_results.json"); VER = J("18_Verification", "verification_status.json")
DRC = J("07_KiCad_Schematics", "drc_summary.json"); DRC_P = json.load(open(os.path.join(REPO, "hardware", "kicad", "drc_summary.json"))) if os.path.exists(os.path.join(REPO, "hardware", "kicad", "drc_summary.json")) else None
nom = V["nominal"]; xf = V["transformer"]; ind = V["inductor"]; spec = V["spec"]
R = []; w = R.append
w("# Research, Design, Optimization and Implementation of a 6.6 kW High-Efficiency Bidirectional Silicon Carbide Dual Active Bridge DC-DC Converter for Industrial High-Voltage Power Conversion Using Advanced Soft-Switching and Adaptive Digital Control\n")
w(f"_Technical report generated from the project result files on {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d')}. All quantitative results are analytical or simulated unless a laboratory record is cited; no hardware has been built or measured._\n")
w("## 1. Abstract\n")
w(f"This report documents the complete, reproducible engineering chain of a {spec['P']/1e3:.1f} kW bidirectional dual active bridge (DAB) converter between an {spec['V1_min']:.0f}-{spec['V1_max']:.0f} V industrial DC bus and a {spec['V2_min']:.0f}-{spec['V2_max']:.0f} V DC port, "
  f"built with 1200 V SiC MOSFETs on both bridges at {spec['fs']/1e3:.0f} kHz. Starting from an existing 3 kW phase-shifted full-bridge (PSFB) reference design, the topology is selected by a quantitative comparison (PSFB, DAB, CLLLC, interleaved and three-phase DAB), the power stage is designed analytically "
  f"(series inductance {V['L']*1e6:.0f} uH, n = {spec['n']:.0f}, E65 transformer, gapped E55 inductor), the losses and junction temperatures are modelled over the full voltage/power envelope (calculated full-load efficiency {100*nom['eta']:.2f} %, peak {100*V['eta_peak']:.2f} %), and the design is validated by a closed-loop switched-model simulation and an ngspice switching-level model "
  f"(power {SP['P_in_W']/1e3:.2f} kW vs {spec['P']/1e3:.1f} kW analytical, ZVS at all eight edges). A digital controller (PI with modulator-inverse feedforward, EPS voltage matching, TPS option, explicit MPC alternative) is designed, implemented in portable C for a TI C2000 target and tested software-in-the-loop "
  f"({'all checks pass' if VER and all(r['status'] != 'FAIL' for r in VER if 'SIL' in r['check']) else 'see verification report'}). A hierarchical KiCad schematic (259 components) and a 6-layer PCB with three isolation regions are generated from a single design database, DRC-checked against IEC 60664-1-derived clearance rules; "
  "thermal, EMI/EMC, insulation coordination, FMEA, optimisation, manufacturing outputs and a staged laboratory plan complete the package. The contribution is methodological (an open, tool-verified design chain); no experimental results are claimed.\n")
w("## 2. Introduction\n")
w("Isolated bidirectional DC-DC conversion is the enabling block of industrial DC microgrids, HVDC distribution inside plants and battery-energy-storage interfaces [1]-[5], [19]. Silicon carbide MOSFETs allow 100 kHz operation at 850 V with low switching loss [20], but the designer must handle the voltage-ratio-dependent loss of zero-voltage switching, high dv/dt, insulation coordination at 850 V and a digital controller with hardware-independent protection. This package addresses these points for a concrete 6.6 kW, 800 V / 400 V design.\n")
w("## 3. Industrial application background\n")
w("The converter is specified (00_Requirements) for a cabinet-mounted module between a 650-850 V DC bus and a 300-450 V DC port (battery string or LVDC feeder), pollution degree 2, overvoltage category II, <= 2000 m, -10 to +45 C full power, forced-air cooling, CAN supervision, with external precharge contactors. The regulated port and the external source/load characteristics are defined explicitly (APP-03/04) so that the control design is not based on silent assumptions.\n")
w("## 4. Research motivation\n")
w("Published DAB work is extensive [1]-[14]; what is rarely available is a complete, reproducible chain from analytical model to routed PCB and firmware in which every number can be regenerated. The motivation here is engineering rigour and traceability (requirements -> calculation -> simulation -> implementation -> verification), on a design point (6.6 kW, 850 V) relevant to industrial HVDC.\n")
w("## 5. Literature review\n")
w("See `01_Literature_Review/literature_review.md` (38 entries: DAB fundamentals and modulation [1]-[14], alternative topologies [15]-[19], SiC devices and drivers [20]-[24], magnetics [25]-[29], control [30]-[31], standards [32]-[38]). The references were recalled from memory and must be cross-checked against the publishers before citation in a submitted thesis; no DOI has been invented.\n")
w("## 6. Research gap\n")
w("The gap addressed is not a new topology or modulation but the absence of openly reproducible, tool-verified engineering packages at this power/voltage class in which the analytical, simulation, firmware and PCB artefacts are generated from one source and checked automatically. The limitations of this software-only study (no measurements, device data flagged for verification) are stated in chapter 23.\n")
w("## 7. Research objectives\n")
w("1. Select and justify the topology for the industrial specification. 2. Derive and implement the DAB models (SPS/EPS/DPS/TPS, ZVS, losses). 3. Design the power stage with a feasibility/derating map. 4. Validate by switched and SPICE simulation. 5. Design and implement the digital control with SIL verification. 6. Generate a DRC-clean, isolation-coordinated PCB. 7. Quantify thermal, EMI and safety aspects. 8. Explore the design space (Pareto). 9. Provide manufacturing and test documentation with an honest verification matrix.\n")
w("## 8. Topology comparison\n")
w(f"`02_Topology_Comparison/` evaluates the candidates at the nine (V1, V2) corners. The PSFB fails the bidirectionality requirement; the CLLLC cannot cover the gain window {min(r['d'] for r in T['rows']):.2f}-{max(r['d'] for r in T['rows']):.2f} with frequency control; the single-phase DAB reaches full power at all corners with |phi| <= 60 deg except 650/300 V, keeps the HV-side rms current between {min(r['Irms1'] for r in T['rows'] if r['Irms1']==r['Irms1']):.1f} and {max(r['Irms1'] for r in T['rows'] if r['Irms1']==r['Irms1']):.1f} A, and scores highest in the weighted matrix (industrial suitability, cost, fault robustness). The interleaved two-phase DAB is the documented fallback.\n")
w("## 9. Selected converter architecture\n")
w(f"Single-phase DAB: HV bridge 4 x {V['dev1']}, LV bridge 4 x {V['dev2']}, n = {spec['n']:.0f} (E65/32/27 3C95, {xf['N1']}:{xf['N2']}), series inductance {V['L']*1e6:.0f} uH ({xf['Llk']*1e6:.1f} uH leakage + {V['L_ext']*1e6:.0f} uH external E55), HV link 4 x 20 uF/1100 V film, LV link 4 x 30 uF/700 V, four UCC21520 reinforced isolated drivers with eight isolated +15/-3 V bias modules, AMC1301 isolated sensing, CT inductor-current sense, LM393 hardware protection, TI F280049C control via LaunchPad, 24 V auxiliary input, CAN/UART.\n")
w("## 10. Mathematical modeling\n")
w("Chapter source: `03_Mathematical_Models/dab_mathematical_model.md`, implementation `dabtools/dab/dab_model.py`. The SPS closed forms (power, switching currents, ZVS boundaries) are reproduced numerically to < 0.1 % by the generic three-level waveform engine that also serves EPS/DPS/TPS. The averaged model (current source K_phi into C2 || R with 1.5 Ts delay) is the control plant.\n")
w("## 11. SiC semiconductor analysis\n")
w(f"Device parameters (`dabtools/dab/devices.py`, flagged verified=False) feed conduction (Rds(Tj)), ZVS turn-off (k_zvs = 0.35 of datasheet Eoff, an explicit assumption), hard-switching (Eon + Eoff + Coss energy where the ZVS criterion fails), dead-time diode and gate losses. At 800/400 V, 6.6 kW: HV bridge {nom['losses']['HV bridge conduction']+nom['losses']['HV bridge switching (ZVS turn-off)']+nom['losses']['HV bridge dead-time diode']:.1f} W, LV bridge {nom['losses']['LV bridge conduction']+nom['losses']['LV bridge switching (ZVS turn-off)']+nom['losses']['LV bridge dead-time diode']:.1f} W, Tj {nom['Tj1']:.0f} / {nom['Tj2']:.0f} C at 45 C ambient. Worst-case stresses: 850 V / 1200 V (71 %), peak current {max(c['Ipk1'] for c in V['corners'] if c['Ipk1']==c['Ipk1']):.1f} A HV side at the corners, design envelope limit {V['I_limit_pk']:.0f} A, hardware trip {V['I_trip_hw']:.0f} A.\n")
w("## 12. Soft-switching analysis\n")
w(f"The energy criterion with Coss(er) gives minimum switching currents I_min = {nom['Imin1']:.2f} A (HV) and {nom['Imin2']:.2f} A (LV); ZVS maps over (V1, V2, P) are in `04_Design_Calculations/img/derating_map.png`: with SPS full ZVS holds down to ~{100*min(x for row in V['derating']['zvs_sps'] for x in row if x==x):.0f}-{100*max(x for row in V['derating']['zvs_sps'] for x in row if x==x):.0f} % load depending on the ratio; EPS/TPS extend it (chapter 14). The ngspice model confirms ZVS at all eight edges at the nominal point (v_DS at turn-on < 0.5 % of the link voltage) and shows the dead-time effect on the effective phase ({SP['phase_loss_deg_equivalent']:.1f} deg per edge, compensated in firmware).\n")
w("## 13. High-frequency magnetics design\n")
w(f"`06_Magnetics/magnetics_design.md`: core comparison (E55/ETD59/E65/PQ65/E70 x 3C95/N97), selected E65 pair, {xf['N1']}:{xf['N2']} litz ({xf['strands1']}/{xf['strands2']} x 0.1 mm), Bpk {xf['Bpk']:.3f} T, core loss {xf['P_core']:.1f} W, copper {xf['P_cu']:.1f} W (Dowell/litz), leakage {xf['Llk']*1e6:.1f} uH interleaved vs {V['transformer_integrated_leakage']['Llk']*1e6:.1f} uH non-interleaved (integrated-leakage option rejected for tolerance reasons), reinforced tape insulation, test procedure. Inductor: E55 gapped {ind['gap']*1e3:.2f} mm, {ind['N']} turns, {ind['P_total']:.1f} W.\n")
w("## 14. Digital control development\n")
w(f"`11_Control_Algorithms/`: power-normalised PI (kp = {C['kp']:.0f} W/V, ki = {C['ki']:.3g} W/(V s)) with modulator inverse in current form, crossover {C['fc']:.0f} Hz, phase margin {C['pm']:.0f} deg including the 1.5 Ts delay; EPS voltage matching (D = d) as default modulation, TPS by numerical search as option, explicit one-step MPC as research alternative (dip 0.13 V vs 2.7 V for PI on the averaged model). Firmware (`10_Firmware/`): portable C core + C2000 HAL; the SIL harness exposed two real defects during development (soft-start reference from 0 V, period-end instead of peak current) which were fixed in both implementations.\n")
w("## 15. Simulation methodology\n")
w(f"Three model levels: analytical waveform engine; closed-loop switched model in Python (ideal switches, R_s = 0.3 Ohm loop resistance, link capacitors with bus/battery models, controller in the loop at 100 kHz); ngspice netlist with behavioural switches, body diodes and Coss. Results: start-up overshoot {SW['startup']['overshoot_pct']:.2f} %, 50 % load-step dip {SW['load_step']['dip_pct']:.2f} %, 10 % HV dip -> V2 within {SW['v1_dip']['v2_min']:.1f}-{SW['v1_dip']['v2_max']:.1f} V, reversal without fault, dead-bus start at {SW['dead_bus_start']['ipk_max']:.1f} A peak; SPICE {SP['P_in_W']:.0f} W, I_rms {SP['iL_rms']:.2f} A vs {V['nominal']['Irms1']:.2f} A analytical.\n")
w("## 16. PCB engineering\n")
w("`07_KiCad_Schematics/` holds the KiCad 7 project (schematic 5 sheets + 6-layer PCB generated by `dabtools/kicad_dab/`): regions HV | 16 mm barrier | control | 16 mm barrier | LV, planes HV_N/HV_P, GND, LV_N/LV_P, switch-node strips on B.Cu, gate clusters at the Kelvin-source pins, straddling isolators in barrier cut-outs with slots under the bias modules, DRC rules by net class (1.5 mm HV-HV, 0.5 mm gate, 8/10/12 mm isolation). ")
if DRC:
    w(f"DRC state of the generated board: {DRC['severities'].get('error', 0)} errors, {DRC['unconnected']} unconnected items, kinds {DRC['drc_kinds']}.\n")
else:
    w("DRC state: board generation pending at report build time (see 18_Verification).\n")
w("## 17. Thermal engineering\n")
w("`13_Thermal_Analysis/`: worst-corner bridge losses scaled from the loss model, cooling options from natural convection to cold plate; selected forced air 3 m/s with two 0.22 K/W extrusions (Tj < 70 C at 45 C ambient; margin for 2x model error), derating curve above 55 C, capacitor hot-spot and thermal-cycling notes.\n")
w("## 18. EMI and EMC considerations\n")
w("`14_EMI_EMC/`: DM spectrum from the pulsating bridge current, CM envelope from 20 V/ns edges through ~100 pF per node, required attenuation (DM ~39 dB, CM ~57 dB at 150 kHz-2 MHz vs CISPR 11 class A), two-stage LC filter proposal, layout measures, pre-compliance plan.\n")
w("## 19. Reliability and safety\n")
w("`15_Safety_Reliability/`: insulation coordination (IEC 62477-1 / 60664-1 basis: basic HV-LV at 850 V, reinforced ports-to-control; design distances 9/16 mm; the 3 kVrms brief value is revised to 2.5 kVrms basic + 4 kVrms reinforced tests), protection coordination (hardware OC/OV/driver -> PROT_DIS, firmware, system), FMEA with 19 items and open actions (reinforced-rated bias modules, DESAT drivers, flux-balance detection).\n")
w("## 20. Multi-objective optimization\n")
if OPT:
    b = OPT["baseline"]
    w(f"`12_Optimization/`: exhaustive grid of {OPT['n_candidates']} candidates ({OPT['n_feasible']} feasible) over fs, n, phi_nom, cores, dead time and devices; Pareto front in (loss, magnetics volume) with {len(OPT['pareto'])} non-dominated points; the baseline ({b['P_loss']:.0f} W, {b['vol']:.0f} cm3) sits at the knee; sensitivity plots for fs, phase shift and dead time.\n")
w("## 21. Results and discussion\n")
w(f"| Quantity | Value | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| Series inductance / nominal phase shift | {V['L']*1e6:.0f} uH / {math.degrees(V['phi_nom']):.1f} deg | 04 |\n| HV / LV rms current at nominal | {nom['Irms1']:.1f} / {nom['Irms2']:.1f} A | 04, SPICE {SP['iL_rms']:.1f} A |\n| Calculated efficiency nominal / peak | {100*nom['eta']:.2f} / {100*V['eta_peak']:.2f} % | 04 (analytical) |\n| Full-power envelope | all corners except 650/300 V (phi > 60 deg), see derating map | 04 |\n| ZVS light-load limit (SPS, nominal) | {100*V['derating']['zvs_sps'][4][3]:.0f} % | 04 |\n| Loop crossover / phase margin | {C['fc']:.0f} Hz / {C['pm']:.0f} deg | 11 |\n| 50 % load-step dip | {SW['load_step']['dip_pct']:.2f} % | 05 |\n| SIL tests | {'all pass' if VER and not any(r['status']=='FAIL' and 'SIL' in r['check'] for r in VER) else 'see 18'} | 10/18 |\n")
w("The calculated efficiency is above the objectives, but the loss model inherits unverified device parameters and the k_zvs assumption; published measurements of SiC DABs in this class are typically 97-98 %, so the margin to EL-07 (96.5 %) is plausible while the absolute value is not. The SPS ZVS limit at light load is the main efficiency risk; EPS matching mitigates it at d != 1.\n")
w("## 22. Comparison with published converters\n")
w("Compared with the reference designs in the literature list (Krismer/Kolar automotive DAB [6]-[8] at 2 kW / 100 kHz with Si devices; Inoue/Akagi 20 kHz IGBT DAB [3]; Jung et al. CLLC for DC distribution [18]), this design operates at a higher voltage with SiC and the same fundamental SPS/EPS/TPS trade-offs; its calculated efficiency and the ZVS behaviour versus d are consistent with those publications' trends. A quantitative benchmark requires measurements.\n")
w("## 23. Research limitations\n")
w("No hardware; device parameters from memory (flagged); isolation values recalled from standards (flagged); gate-bias modules only basic-class; BoosterPack pin mapping unverified; KiCad 7 CLI has no ERC (netlist/pin consistency used instead); the generated PCB routing is produced by an own router and is checked by KiCad DRC but has not been reviewed for manufacturability by a human; EMI figures are analytical envelopes.\n")
w("## 24. Experimental validation methodology\n")
w("`20_Experimental_Test_Plan/test_plan.md`: 13 staged tests from bare-board inspection and magnetics characterisation through insulation tests, protection injection, HIL, low-voltage power, staged HV power with ZVS verification, efficiency maps, dynamics, thermal soak, EMI pre-compliance and long-duration run, with instruments, criteria and safety controls.\n")
w("## 25. Future research directions\n")
w("Measured validation and model calibration (k_zvs, Coss nonlinearity); TPS table generation and online adaptation; DESAT-based drivers and reinforced bias supplies; flux-balance observer; integrated-leakage transformer with controlled tolerance; MPC on target with timing measurements; three-phase DAB for 20 kW scaling.\n")
w("## 26. Conclusions\n")
w("A complete, regenerable engineering package for a 6.6 kW SiC DAB has been produced: topology decision, analytical design with envelope maps, two levels of simulation in agreement with the analysis, a SIL-tested control core, a generated schematic and PCB with isolation-coordinated DRC rules, and the supporting thermal/EMI/safety/manufacturing/test documentation. The verification matrix (18) states precisely which checks ran; experimental validation remains to be done under an approved procedure.\n")
w("## 27. References\n\nSee `01_Literature_Review/literature_review.md` (numbered [1]-[38]).\n")
w("## 28. Appendices\n\n* A. Design values: `04_Design_Calculations/design_values.json`, report `design_report.md`\n* B. Simulation results: `05_Simulation/switched_results.json`, `spice/spice_results.json`, `img/`\n* C. Control parameters: `11_Control_Algorithms/control_params.json`\n* D. Optimisation results: `12_Optimization/optimization_results.json`\n* E. Verification evidence: `18_Verification/verification_report.md`, `verification_status.json`, DRC reports `07_KiCad_Schematics/drc_report.txt`\n* F. Requirements traceability: `00_Requirements/03_RTM.csv`\n* G. BOM: `16_BOM/`\n")
open(os.path.join(HERE, "report.md"), "w").write("\n".join(R) + "\n")
print("report.md written,", sum(len(x) for x in R), "chars")
